Package: scbamqc
Title: Cell Selection from Single-Cell Alignment Quality
Version: 0.1.0.9000
Authors@R:
    person("Argenis", "Arriojas", , "ArriojasMaldonado001@umb.edu", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Scores each cell barcode by the kernel density of its
    alignment profile (soft-clipped fraction, base quality) and selects
    cells with a two-component Gaussian mixture on counts and score.
    Reads the per-barcode table written by the 'scbamqc bam' command of the
    Python package. Works on 'Seurat' objects and data frames.
License: BSD_3_clause + file LICENSE
URL: https://github.com/umbibio/scbamqc
BugReports: https://github.com/umbibio/scbamqc/issues
Depends:
    R (>= 4.1)
Imports:
    mclust,
    stats,
    utils
Suggests:
    ggplot2 (>= 3.5.0),
    Matrix,
    SeuratObject,
    testthat (>= 3.0.0)
Config/testthat/edition: 3
